From 1e4daed9bf120b248786a029ef89653a76d0b362 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhengzeying <zhengzeying@canaan-creative.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:04:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/canaan: VFP-timed vblank and computed DSI timings

Rework the Canaan VO/DSI driver for correct frame-base latching and
panel-accurate DSI timing.

VO:
- Report the CRTC vblank from the vertical front porch (active end) via an
  hrtimer armed by the vsync IRQ instead of the 2^n-line interrupt: the
  displayed framebuffer has finished scanning out by then, so it is the
  earliest point at which the old buffer is safe to release.
- Write the frame base directly in the atomic commit (canaan_vo_write_base).
  The base registers are not GO-gated and hardware samples them at the layer
  latch point, so writing them well before the latch keeps all layers in step;
  the VFP hrtimer then only reports the vblank.
- Use auto address mode with base0 == base1 (single buffer) on all layers
  (video2/3 ADDR_SEL 0x00, OSD 0x00, LAYER1 bit16 enable only).
- Enable IRQ0 only when a vblank is subscribed; drop the IRQ0/hrtimer teardown
  race in disable_crtc via synchronize_irq(); note (dev_dbg) when vfp <= 32
  (RDMA prefetch margin).

DSI:
- Compute hsfreqrange, D-PHY LP/HS transition timings, ESC/timeout clock
  dividers and DPI 24-bit colour coding from the lane rate instead of the
  previous hardcoded values.
